      "id": "dhs-icepick-leak",
      "weight": "normal",
      "title": "A leak exposes 41,000 DHS staff, and Bluesky blocks the links",
      "topics": [
        "US",
        "Security",
        "Privacy"
      ],
      "facts": [
        "Distributed Denial of Secrets published an archive, dubbed \"Icepick\", on more than 41,000 DHS employees and contractors, including ICE and CBP staff.",
        "It lists names, email addresses, phone numbers and membership of internal groups, in some cases tied to surveillance and undercover operations, WIRED reports.",
        "A group calling itself the Department of Peace handed the files over. Activists say they took them in a cyberattack, per ZEIT.",
        "Bluesky labels links to the archive \"malicious\" because it shares contact details without authorization. On X, Grok pointed users to a searchable version."
      ],
      "whyItMatters": "It maps who does what inside DHS during an immigration crackdown, and platforms are already splitting on whether to let it spread.",
